  "notes": "This is a first pressing with Capitol grey \"Long Playing\" labels and the front cover variation showing Sinatra facing away from the couple.\n\nSimilar to [r=8124481], which has the same \"Long Playing\" labels, but the later front cover variation of Sinatra looking forward.\nSimilar to [r=2390268], which has \"Long Playing • High Fidelity\" labels, and the later front cover variation of Sinatra looking forward.\n\nThe [Anvil symbol] (\"⌂\") stamped in runouts denotes a [l=Capitol Records Pressing Plant, Scranton], pressing. The remainder of the runouts are mostly stamped.\n\nCatalog number on sleeve: W653\nCatalog number on labels: W-653\n\nTitle on spine, labels: Songs For Swingin' Lovers\n\nIssued in a \"...a word about High Fidelity\" / \"This Protective Envelope\" company inner sleeve that may be stamped or handwritten in blue with \"653.\"\n",
  "released_formatted": "Mar 1956",
